# glob | whom it is about | text
@title Elsewhere
@intro what two other libraries do.
# one member, by the label of one check
Shape.area/circle | Round | takes pi to be 4
# the same remark from another: shown once, with both
Shape.area/circle | Square | takes pi to be 4
# a set, a question mark and a star; the text has a bar, a star and a bracket
Shape.scale/by-[a-z]er? | Round | scale (s, 0) raises Div: k | 0, and *not* [0]
Shape.s*/by-one | Round | scale (s, 1) copies
# a star that runs over the slash
Shape.are* | Flat | has no areas
# a computed label, by the beginning that is known of it
Shape.name/of-sq* | Round | calls a square a box
# a computed label of which nothing is known: only because nothing else has it
Shape.*/thrice | Round | grows three times
# a constructor counts for its datatype
Shape.Circle/is-* | Flat | has no circles
# the structure as a whole against its signature
Shape:SHAPE/* | Flat | is sealed
